Subject: promotes register variables into fixed homes

What this does
  Assigns eligible variables fixed registers and preserves overlapping values
  with explicit copies. It also fixes register aliasing and operand ownership
  assumptions exposed by the backend.

Why we need it
  Phi copies dominate register move traffic. Aliased values at joins and
  handlers that consumed read-only operands made home allocation unsafe until
  those paths were corrected.

What it adds
  Home selection, overlap splitting, register compaction, and checks that
  refuse unsafe functions. It also makes optimization use counts include join
  inputs and retains register ownership for read-only operands.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No. The register function tag and bytecode format change are in 0107.

Notes
  Homes are gated by REGVM_HOMES. Box2D move dispatches fall from 15.55% to
  5.34%.

